"""
sheet_tree_server.py
----------------------
Interactive tree of sheet-to-sheet data flow. Clicking a sheet box
ACTUALLY switches to that sheet in Excel - a plain browser link can't
do this reliably (browsers strip the sheet info when handing a file
off to Excel), so this runs a small local server that uses pywin32
(COM automation - the same mechanism VBA macros use) to control Excel
directly. No Excel add-in required.

Requires:
    pip install openpyxl pywin32
    Excel must be installed (this drives the real Excel application).

Usage:
    python sheet_tree_server.py workbook.xlsx
    python sheet_tree_server.py workbook.xlsx 5      (only show links with 5+ cells)

This opens the tree in your browser automatically and starts a local
server. Leave the terminal window open while you use it - closing it
(Ctrl+C) stops the server. Clicking a sheet box brings Excel to the
front and switches to that sheet.
"""

